# The fusions whose parts carry a conversion nobody sized. One row per such fusion, shaped like the
# two elimination suspensions beside it so the union stays a union.
#
# A derived conversion is said to be one
#   A derivation is an output the receiver computes, not a gap. Nothing yet computes a factor from
#   the rest of the unit graph or from the fusion's sum, so the sum is still lifted, under the
#   identity's name.
#
# The same reason an unsized elimination lifts the sum
#   An unsized conversion lifts the sum for the same reason an unsized elimination does, and the
#   schema already made that argument about the other one: "an entry whose `quantity` takes its
#   absent branch is a composer who found the overlap and could not size it, so the sum is lifted
#   exactly where the elimination was filed." A factor is the other multiplier in
#   `Σ converted parts`. If nobody sized it, the converted part is not a number and the sum it
#   feeds is not owed.
#
# It keeps composition/converted.sqlc from under-counting
#   Without this, the exclusion in composition/converted.sqlc would silently under-count. That
#   relation drops a part whose factor is typed-absent, because converting it by one would assert
#   the units agree, which is the claim the filer declined to make. A dropped part in a sum that
#   still owes equality is a shortfall the checker invented. This is the ground that keeps the two
#   consistent.
#
# The population is already suspended on another ground
#   The population is one, and it is already suspended on another ground.
#   `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` files its elimination search as `unmeasured` too, so
#   no verdict moves on this corpus. This makes structural a thing that is true only by luck,
#   which is the same repair as every CHECK in the DDL.
-- asrt:Part/asrt:factor taking its pm:absent or pm:derivation branch, as a suspension of the composed sum.
SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer,
       NULL::pm.summed_quantity AS quantity,
       CASE WHEN p.factor_state = 'derivation'
            THEN format('the conversion is filed as `%s`, and no computation of it is wired into '
                        'the sum', p.factor_derivation)
            ELSE 'the conversion was filed and could not be sized' END AS suspended_because,
       coalesce(p.factor_absent::text, p.factor_derivation::text) AS note
FROM (
    :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
) p
WHERE p.factor_state IN ('absent', 'derivation')
